{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he said, I will do, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary for him to say this to him, and he should have simply performed the deed in action — and this itself is his answer — as we find also with Eliezer, servant of Abraham, when Abraham said to him (Genesis 24:2): ״שִׂים נָא יָדְךָ״ etc., the response was: ״וַיָּשֶׂם הָעֶבֶד אֶת יָדוֹ״ etc." "<b>However,</b> the intention is that he gave him an answer indicating that he need not swear to him, and behold he is prepared to do according to his words." "<b>Or</b> it may mean that according to the law he is obligated to do according to his words — either because he is his son, and that is what is meant by <b>I will do</b>; or because he is commanding by reason of death (Choshen Mishpat 252:2), and that is what is meant by <b>according to your words</b> — and he does not need an oath. And through this, Yosef, upon him be peace, made known his righteousness, that he desires kindness to perform a matter of mitzvah of his own simple free will."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:47.760273354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}